    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Indus Valley Civilization (IVC) was a Bronze Age civilization known for its advanced urban grid planning and subterranean drainage systems.",
        "Harappa was discovered by Daya Ram Sahni in 1921, and Mohenjo-daro was excavated by R.D. Banerji in 1922 under Sir John Marshall.",
        "Major agricultural produce included wheat, barley, cotton, and sesame, with Lothal serving as a major international port city.",
        "Religious practices centered around the worship of Proto-Shiva (Pashupati), Mother Goddess, and natural elements without monumental temples.",
        "The Harappan script remains undeciphered to date and was written in a boustrophedon style (right to left and left to right in alternate lines)."
      ],
      "id": "0zl2ese"
    },
